    "href": "index.html",
    "title": "Building Community-Engaged Statistics and Data Science (CESDS) Courses",
    "section": "",
    "text": "GETTING STARTED\nThis handbook provides resources for developing and teaching community-engaged statistics and data science (CESDS) courses at the undergraduate level.\nWe define community-engaged statistics and data science (CESDS) courses as…\nThe handbook covers both the development and implementation of CESDS courses, including course design, project scoping, community partnerships, student project work, ethical considerations, common challenges, and project handoff and sustainability.\nThe handbook is being developed during the 2026-2027 academic year by a working group. More information about the project and working group is available on the CESDS website. Check back to learn more!",
    "crumbs": [
      "GETTING STARTED"
    ]
  },
