    "title": "Building Community-Engaged Statistics and Data Science (CESDS) Courses",
    "section": "Acknowledgments",
    "text": "Acknowledgments\nDevelopment of this handbook is supported by the RIOS Institute (Institute for a Racially Just, Inclusive, and Open STEM Education). RIOS funding supports the 2026-2027 working group and stipends for participating members.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTipTips for Authors\n\n\n\nThis section is for contributors and will be removed from the final handbook.\nThis handbook is built using Quarto. Below are some Quarto features that may be useful as you add content.\n\nHeadings\nUse headings to organize sections within your chapter. They will appear automatically in the page table of contents.\n## Main section\n\n### Subsection\n\n\nCitations\nUse @citationkey to cite sources and add the corresponding BibTeX entry to references.bib.\nThis approach has been used in previous work @knuth84.\n\n\nLinks\nCreate descriptive links rather than displaying a full URL.\nLearn more from the [RIOS Institute](https://qubeshub.org/community/groups/ri\n\n\nCallouts\nCallouts can be used for examples, notes, or other information you want to distinguish from the main text.\nSee examples of call-outs below.\n::: {.callout-note}\nAdd information here.\n\n\nCross-references\nAdd an ID to a section.\n## Learning Objectives {#sec-learning-objectives}\nThen link to it elsewhere using, see @sec-learning-objectives.\n\n\nComments\nUse HTML comments for notes between authors that should not appear in the rendered handbook:\n&lt;!-- TODO: Add an example here. --&gt;\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNote\n\n\n\nAdd information here.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWarning\n\n\n\nAdd cautionary tale here.\n\n\nLearn more about types of Callout Blocks at quarto.org. They can also be collapsible.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNoteExample\n\n\n\n\n\nAdd an example here.\n\n\n\nSupplemental or sidenote information can be placed in the margin.\n\n\n\n\nAdd a perspective here.",
